Z||000002||DaRkLoRD||04-28-2001||05:02 AM||||LOL<P>"opped" means you have operator status... gives you the ability to kick people from the channel, to set the mode, etc. on a real IRC server, it'd also allow you to change the topic, ban people, etc<P>it's like having control over the channel..<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||10
Z||000003||fropuff||04-28-2001||01:33 PM||||If you're talking about where it says:  [sqoach opped by server hax.spin.de], that means that there are no other people in the chat room at the time.  When it says that for me, I just leave it on until other people enter the chat room.  <P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000004||fropuff||04-28-2001||01:37 PM||||By the way, last night I found out that when you enter the name of the room, it is case sensitive.  _fiero.nl is a different chat than _Fiero.nl.  If you type in _fiero.nl, you're going to get the opped message every time, because everyone else types in _Fiero.nl.  Understand?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
